Package: x11-xvfb
Name: Xvfb (virtual framebuffer X server)
Version: 1.20.11+rootless1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Depends: libxfont2, libpixman-1-0, libxau6, libxdmcp6, libiosexec1 (>= 1.3.1), libmd0, xkbcomp, xkeyboard-config, xauth
Provides: xvfb
Conflicts: xvfb
Replaces: xvfb
Section: X11
Priority: optional
Description: Virtual framebuffer X server for rootless jailbreaks
 Xvfb is a headless X11 server that renders to an in-memory framebuffer instead
 of real graphics hardware. This is the same Xvfb from xorg-server 1.20.11
 (as bundled with TigerVNC), rebuilt from source for rootless /var/jb and
 ad-hoc signed.
 .
 Stock X servers crash on startup under rootless because XKB init spawns its
 xkbcomp helper through /bin/sh, which does not exist on a rootless jailbreak
 (the shell lives at /var/jb/bin/sh). This build fixes the spawn path so
 keyboard init succeeds with no on-device hacks.
 .
 Use it for headless/debug X11 sessions or software-only bring-up. The public
 Xios app display path uses the IOSurface Xios server instead. Pair with a window
 manager (fluxbox), xterm, and the x11-fonts-sf package. Built for iPadOS/iOS
 rootless (palera1n/Dopamine, /var/jb).
